<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- The swapchain tests create a real Win32 window through LibraryImport, which the source
         generator emits unsafe code for. There is nothing to mock: DXGI validates the HWND. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../../src/OpenMCAD.Render/OpenMCAD.Render.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>


  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Test collections run one at a time in this assembly.

      Originally because every class here created its own D3D12 device, and xunit runs collections
      in parallel by default, so several WARP devices with the debug layer attached were being
      created and destroyed concurrently, which crashed the test host with an access violation in
      roughly a third of runs and never when a single class was run on its own.

      Most of that is gone: the passes now share one device for the whole assembly (TestDevices),
      and only the three classes that are *about* the device lifecycle still make their own. This
      stays anyway, because those three would still be creating and destroying devices alongside
      the shared one, and because there was never anything to gain from the parallelism: the whole
      assembly takes a few seconds, and the GPU serialises the work regardless of how many threads
      ask it to.

      Same arrangement, for the same kind of reason, as OpenMCAD.Kernel.Contract.Tests.
    -->
    <Content Include="xunit.runner.json" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
